# QUESTION: Does a real ze hub open Warning alarm config-resync-failed (and not
# config-rejected) when both diff resync and full replay fail with a non-verify
# error, hide it behind device-offline while the device is disconnected with
# | hidden true selection, and clear both alarms while retaining overlap history
# once a reconnect resync converges?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: Alarm kind registration in the shipped ze hub binary,
# hub-side managed session diff/full/ack handling, offline-delay expiry,
# same-device cause hiding, disk ZeFS alarm history persistence, and SSH CLI
# show fleet alarm pipe filtering run end to end through the real ze hub daemon.
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-10 AC-1, AC-2, R-11.
option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=180s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture managed/fleet-resync-failed-alarm $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=180s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: fleet resync-failed alarm opened on non-verify failure, hid behind device-offline, and cleared on convergence
